.TH OCTA-AUTO-SENSE 1 "" "OCTA-CAPTURE @PROJECT_VERSION@" "OCTA-CAPTURE Manual"
.SH NAME
octa\-auto\-sense \- run selected-input sensitivity calibration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBocta-auto-sense\fR [\fB\-\-interactive\fR] MASK DURATION-MS finish|cancel NEW-RECOVERY.syx [CTRL-PORT]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run Auto-Sens for a decimal channel bitmask 1..255 (bit 0 selects input 1).
DURATION-MS is 1..60000. Create a new durable raw recovery snapshot before changes;
refuse an existing recovery file. This changes preamp sensitivity.
The finish action keeps the result; cancel restores the complete raw pre-start state.
.PP
Interactive mode emits readiness events; SIGUSR1 requests Finish and SIGTERM
requests Cancel. Unresolved completion is reported as failure; keep the recovery file.
.PP
The default CTRL MIDI port is hw:CARD=OCTACAPTURE,DEV=0,SUBDEV=1. Close other control-panel/CTRL clients before opening it. Audio streaming is independent of this connection.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success; nonzero indicates a usage, device or operation error.
.SH SEE ALSO
octa-capture(1), octa-status(1), octa-preset(1)
